$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=tm2lrnenc  LOC_AFTER=?

* The entry-size bound of an encoded list from the value bound: every entry of ` ( encNatGam o. L ) ` has at most ` B ` bits when every value of ` L ` is below ` 2 ^ B ` .  Lean: ` entry_length_le_of_lt_pow ` .

s1::simp1 |- ( ( L e. Word NN0 /\ B e. NN0 /\ A. a e. ran L a < ( 2 ^ B ) ) -> L e. Word NN0 )
s2::simp2 |- ( ( L e. Word NN0 /\ B e. NN0 /\ A. a e. ran L a < ( 2 ^ B ) ) -> B e. NN0 )
s3::simp3 |- ( ( L e. Word NN0 /\ B e. NN0 /\ A. a e. ran L a < ( 2 ^ B ) ) -> A. a e. ran L a < ( 2 ^ B ) )
s4::tm2lbitf |- encNatGam : NN0 --> Word ( { 1 } X. 2o )
i5::ffn
s6:s4,i5:ax-mp |- encNatGam Fn NN0
s7:s6:a1i |- ( ( L e. Word NN0 /\ B e. NN0 /\ A. a e. ran L a < ( 2 ^ B ) ) -> encNatGam Fn NN0 )
i8::wrdf
s9:s1,i8:syl |- ( ( L e. Word NN0 /\ B e. NN0 /\ A. a e. ran L a < ( 2 ^ B ) ) -> L : ( 0 ..^ ( # ` L ) ) --> NN0 )
